}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kaoru Hanayama CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Boasting both [[Massive Damage]] and [[Resistant|Resistance]] vs. Aku, along with a 100% chance to instantly destroy [[Shield]]s, Hanayama is an extraordinarily impressive [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku]] specialist. Despite his mediocre standing range and abysmally long foreswing animation of nearly 4 seconds (which may lead to him missing, but also gives other enemies a chance to walk into his range), his extremely high damage per hit is beyond compensation and his guaranteed Shield Piercing is just the cherry on top. At level 50, his damage is even enough to instantly kill a 200% [[Midnite D.]]. It is worth keeping in mind that his terribly slow attack rate creates significant downtime during which enemies can pick him off, if he's not timed precisely.

Even then, Hanayama also has more than enough effective HP to tank an absurd amount of punishment—far exceeding even that of [[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Hevijak]]. While one might assume that his singular knockback would limit his usage against target traits, it actually gives him phenomenal bulk, enough to shrug off attacks from buffed [[Fallen Bear]]s, [[Deathkory]], [[Medu-san]] and [[Le'Behemoth]] so he could get a hit on them, destroying them in a few hits at most. It can, however, become an issue in mixed stages, as his [[Immune to Knockback|Knockback]] and [[Immune to Warp|Warp Immunities]] prevent him from repositioning at all. Fortunately, his wide array of immunities do improve his matchups against [[High Priest Mamon]], [[Wicked Face]], [[THE FOLIVOREAN]], [[Ackey]] and [[Cerberus Kids]] whenever relevant.

Overall, Hanayama is a phenomenal anti-Aku nuker, with an impressive set of abilities that make him viable at any point in progression.

{{Job|Classification = Nuker & Tanker}}

